Seren: Replace Bolt/Timestamp with Lolanthe/Verdant and implement both ultimates

Work directly against the current hiyroscript/seren repository. Do not treat this as a greenfield implementation. First inspect the existing architecture, especially js/data.js, js/runtime.js, js/mechanics.js, js/race.js, js/render.js, js/ai.js, js/input.js, js/hud.js, js/i18n.js, js/ui.js, js/main.js, index.html, the tools/*.mjs test harnesses, and the architecture/QA documentation.

The repository already contains these required assets at the project root:

v_lolanthe.PNG
v_verdant.PNG
queen_note.PNG
pion_note.PNG

Do not generate substitute artwork and do not use procedural Bolt/Timestamp bodies after this change.

1. Architectural constraints that must be preserved

Seren currently has a shared ultimate lifecycle. Preserve it.

Every car still uses the existing shared:

ULT_CHARGE = 75 seconds
ULT_TIME = 15 seconds
ULT_SPEED = 2.0

Do not create separate ultimate clocks or an alternate parallel ultimate state machine for Lolanthe or Verdant. Follow the existing Flann/Neela pattern: the shared startUlt(), tickUlt(), and endUlt() lifecycle remains authoritative, while named racer-specific predicates and small state fields implement the extra behavior.

The field must remain six cars. Lolanthe replaces Bolt and Verdant replaces Timestamp. Do not add a seventh or eighth vehicle.

Rendering must remain read-only. Gameplay state and timers must advance from the update/mechanics code, not from rendering functions.

Continue using the existing invariant that the model being drawn is also the model being collided. racerModel(), racerDims(), and carHit() must stay consistent.

Do not break split-screen/local multiplayer. Anything based on visibility must be evaluated per view using the existing view owner concept (VOWN), while gameplay collision/state remains shared globally.

