4. Measure both new PNG models properly

Do not copy Flann’s or Neela’s geometry.

Inspect v_lolanthe.PNG and v_verdant.PNG and measure the actual artwork.

For each vehicle, determine the actual visible-body pixel bounds in the PNG and store normalized spriteBounds exactly as the existing Flann/Neela sprite system expects.

Measure the center of every actual rear tailpipe/exhaust outlet and store those as normalized exhaust anchors. Boost fire must visibly originate from the actual tailpipe mouths at all race scales, tilts, screen sizes, and split-screen column widths.

Both cars should use the normal sprite flame path, not Neela’s energy exhaust, unless the artwork itself makes a different treatment clearly necessary. The user’s requirement is boost fire from the actual tailpipe.

Trace a precise polygonal hitShape around each visible vehicle body. Do not give either car the generic CAR_HIT_RECT. Exclude transparent padding and non-body trailing visual details in the same way Neela/Flann geometry is currently measured.

If a raceScale adjustment is necessary to make the visible body occupy a sensible amount of the lane, derive it from the measured image rather than guessing. Keep scaling uniform so artwork, hitbox, sprite bounds, and exhaust anchors remain aligned.

Extend tools/sprite-check.mjs and tools/hitbox-check.mjs so these measurements become regressions rather than undocumented visual guesses.

