The Condition description must communicate that the racer loses control for three seconds and that a new application resets the timer rather than stacking additional duration.

Every racer, including player one and rival/local-human racer objects, needs a mind-control timer such as mindT.

Add:

MIND_CONTROL_TIME = 3

or an equivalently named tuning constant in the shared tuning/data layer.

conditionOn() must derive the Condition directly from mindT > 0.

clearDebuffs() must clear mindT.

The existing invulnerability/dead/finished debuff refusal rules must apply. A racer that refuses debuffs must not receive mind control, and becoming protected must clear it consistently with the rest of Seren’s debuffs.

8. Mind-control timer reset semantics

Applying mind control must set:

target.mindT = MIND_CONTROL_TIME

It must never do:

target.mindT += MIND_CONTROL_TIME

Repeated application resets the timer to three seconds. It does not stack to six, nine, twelve seconds, etc.

If a target remains continuously inside Lolanthe’s aura, repeated application can keep resetting the timer to three seconds. Therefore the racer can remain controlled for the duration of exposure and then remain controlled for up to three seconds after the last application.

Do not replay the “pop in” animation every frame while the timer is merely being reset. The pop-in is for the inactive → active transition.

9. Lolanthe ultimate aura

