“Nearby” must be implemented as one named, tunable range rather than a magic number scattered through code. Use a distance equivalent to roughly four car lengths along the road. Make it scale correctly with the game rather than tying it to one hardcoded viewport size.

The aura reaches racers in any of the three lanes. Lane does not determine whether a racer becomes Mind Controlled; lane only determines whether the forced “move aside” behavior happens.

Use shared/master race coordinates or an absolute racer-distance helper. The answer must not depend on which split-screen view happens to be rendering.

Skip:

Lolanthe itself
wrecked racers
finished racers
racers currently refusing debuffs
an ulting Verdant

The Verdant immunity is absolute for the whole time Verdant’s ultimate is active, including during Verdant’s brief collision reveal.

10. Lolanthe forced-lane behavior

Whenever a racer affected by Lolanthe’s aura is in the same logical lane as Lolanthe, Lolanthe forces that racer out of the lane.

This is not normal driver steering. It must happen even though the victim is Mind Controlled and its ordinary controls are locked.

From an outer lane, there is only one valid destination and the victim must move inward.

From the middle lane, choose left or right without treating occupancy as a reason to cancel. A stable random choice or similarly unbiased one-time choice is acceptable.

Crucially, do not require the destination lane to be empty.

If there is another racer in the forced destination lane, route the situation through Seren’s real racer-contact/barge resolution rather than teleporting one model through another. The forced movement can therefore shove, wreck, ram, or otherwise interact with the racer already occupying that lane according to the normal special-contact rules.

This is intentionally capable of producing chain reactions and racers destroying one another.

A forced lane move should change the logical lane immediately and then use Seren’s existing lateral interpolation so the car visibly transitions rather than teleports sideways.

The forced movement must ignore things such as Skidded steering reversal because this is Lolanthe commanding the vehicle, not the driver steering it.

Do not let the ordinary mind-control input lock accidentally block Lolanthe’s forced movement. Give forced movement its own internal path.

11. Complete control lock during Mind Controlled

For the entire three-second Mind Controlled duration, the affected driver must be unable to issue meaningful actions.

This must work identically for:

player one
bots
local multiplayer humans

Block manual steering.

Block starting or maintaining an active driver-controlled boost. The car should not continue consuming boost because the player happened to be holding the button when control was taken.

Block firing a new ultimate.

Block using an item.

Block bot lane-choice/action decisions.

Block bot item use and bot ultimate activation.

Do not freeze the racer in space. Its vehicle physics, ordinary forward movement, timed effects, collision handling, active ultimate clock, hazards, wreck lifecycle, and other passive race-state updates should continue.

If a racer was already in an ultimate before becoming Mind Controlled, do not arbitrarily cancel that existing ultimate. The driver simply cannot initiate actions while controlled.

Centralize the “controls are locked” question so one input surface cannot accidentally bypass the restriction.

Do not rely only on suppressing keyboard events. The mechanics-level actions themselves must refuse player commands during mind control.

