19. Directional Verdant collision rule

This rule is asymmetric.

If another racer initiates contact into an ulting Verdant, that attacking/arriving racer is destroyed and Verdant survives.

If an ulting Verdant initiates an ordinary collision into another racer, Verdant must not gain an offensive kill. Use the ordinary contact behavior unless one of the explicit special pair interactions below applies.

The current code already exposes contact direction in the important places:

rearEnd(who, victim) knows which racer ran into the back of which racer.

bumpTarget(victim, dir, by) knows which racer initiated a lane barge.

Use that directionality rather than trying to infer it later from overlapping polygons.

Centralize the special-contact resolution so rearEnd() and bumpTarget() cannot disagree about Verdant.

Preserve invulnerability/dead/finished contact gates. An unreachable racer does not become a free Verdant kill merely because polygons overlap.

20. Special case: ulting Verdant vs ulting Flann

If an ulting Verdant and an ulting Flann physically collide, both racers are destroyed.

This overrides Flann’s normal one-sided ram behavior.

It must apply regardless of which one initiated the contact.

After the collision, both racers’ ultimate meters must be exactly 0%.

Do not allow the standard kill reward or wreck penalty sequencing to leave either meter above zero.

Prefer a small dedicated mutual-wreck resolver that uses the existing wreck lifecycle/FX/audio but guarantees zero fuel after all meter side effects.

Do not let one wreck make the second racer unreachable before the second wreck is processed.

21. Special case: transformed Neela vs ulting Verdant

If Neela is currently in the vtm_neela.PNG alternate/heat-seeking form and physically contacts an ulting Verdant, Neela is destroyed.

This overrides Neela’s normal exchange/swap behavior.

It applies regardless of which of the two vehicles initiated the physical contact.

Neela’s ultimate fuel must become exactly 0%.

Verdant survives.

Trigger Verdant’s brief reveal because physical contact occurred.

Do not teleport either racer using Neela’s swap path.

A normal, non-transformed Neela does not receive this special handling beyond Verdant’s ordinary directional-defense rule.

22. Collision-resolution priority

