36. Acceptance criteria

The implementation is complete only when all of the following are true:

* Bolt is fully replaced as a car by Lolanthe, using v_lolanthe.PNG, and Timestamp is fully replaced as a car by Verdant, using v_verdant.PNG.
* The field remains exactly six vehicles.
* Both PNG cars use measured spriteBounds, measured tailpipe anchors, and precise polygon hitboxes derived from their own artwork.
* Boost fire visibly originates from the correct Lolanthe and Verdant tailpipes.
* Both vehicles retain the shared 75-second charge, 15-second duration, and 2× ultimate pace.
* Lolanthe continuously Mind Controls nearby valid racers during its ultimate.
* Mind Control lasts three seconds from the most recent application and resets rather than stacking.
* Player, bot, and local-human driver actions are all locked while Mind Controlled.
* A racer sharing Lolanthe’s lane is forcibly moved to an adjacent valid lane even when that lane is occupied.
* Forced movement routes through the real collision system and can therefore cause chain collisions/wrecks.
* queen_note.PNG appears above ulting Lolanthe with pop-in, continuous vertical bob, and pop-out.
* Exactly three pion_note.PNG icons orbit every Mind Controlled racer with pop-in/pop-out and no vertical bob.
* An ulting Verdant is physically present with its precise hitbox despite being invisible.
* Verdant is 0% visible in other racers’ views and 50% visible in its own driver’s view.
* Verdant fades into and out of its ultimate visibility state.
* An ordinary racer that initiates contact into ulting Verdant is destroyed and Verdant briefly becomes visible.
* Ulting Verdant does not offensively destroy an ordinary racer merely by initiating contact into it.
* Ulting Verdant + ulting Flann destroys both and leaves both ultimate meters at exactly 0%.
* Transformed vtm_neela.PNG Neela contacting ulting Verdant destroys Neela, leaves Neela’s ultimate at exactly 0%, does not perform the Neela swap, and Verdant survives.
* Ulting Verdant is immune to Lolanthe Mind Control even during its brief reveal.
* Lolanthe and Verdant clear exactly the same solid-hazard class Neela clears while their ultimates are active.
* Existing Flann and Neela mechanics continue to work, including the existing Neela-vs-Flann priority when Verdant is not involved.
* Invisible Verdant does not leak its exact world position through car-attached exhaust, badges, seat markers, or equivalent positional visuals in another player’s view.
* Bots do not deliberately target invisible Verdant using information a human could not see.
* All six cars still work as player, bot, and eligible local-multiplayer selections.
* All localization keys resolve in both languages.
* node tools/check.mjs passes.
* node tools/menu-check.mjs passes.
* node tools/ultimate-check.mjs passes.
* node tools/sprite-check.mjs passes.
* node tools/hitbox-check.mjs passes.
* Manual browser QA confirms correct animations, sprite scaling, tailpipe alignment, collision directionality, Verdant per-view opacity, and two-/three-/four-player split-screen behavior.

Implement this conservatively. Reuse Seren’s current abstractions instead of creating duplicate systems, keep gameplay state deterministic and testable, and do not “solve” invisibility by disabling physical collision or “solve” Mind Control by bypassing the real collision system.
